        { "id": "prt_02b", "sessionID": "ses_08", "messageID": "msg_02", "type": "text", "text": "That's a good implementation task, but not really a user story - it describes a schema change (the \"how\") rather than the need it serves (the \"what\" and \"why\"). A user story usually follows something like \"As a [role], I want [capability], so that [benefit]\", and stays silent on how it's built. The `pinned` column is one valid way to implement it, but the story shouldn't lock that in." },
        { "id": "prt_02c", "sessionID": "ses_08", "messageID": "msg_02", "type": "step-finish", "reason": "stop", "cost": 0.02, "tokens": { "input": 1300, "output": 380, "reasoning": 0, "cache": { "read": 0, "write": 0 } } }
