        { "id": "prt_04b", "sessionID": "ses_08", "messageID": "msg_04", "type": "text", "text": "Exactly right. \"Add a `pinned` boolean column\" is a design/implementation decision - it belongs in a task or a technical design doc, made once you know the requirement. The requirement is the underlying need: moderators want important posts to stay visible at the top of a topic. Try: \"As a moderator, I want to pin an important post to the top of a topic, so that other users see it first.\" Then acceptance criteria like \"a pinned post stays first regardless of reply order\" and \"only one post per topic can be pinned at a time\" - those constrain the behavior without dictating the schema." },
